<h1>Roller Conveyors: Types, Applications &amp; Specifications</h1>
<p class="usa-intro">A roller conveyor uses a series of cylindrical rollers mounted between side frames to transport flat-bottomed products such as cases, cartons, totes, and pallets. Roller conveyors come in five primary types: gravity (unpowered), belt-driven live roller (BDLR), line-shaft, motor driven roller (MDR), and chain-driven live roller (CDLR). They are a standard choice for unit loads in packaging and distribution facilities.</p>
